<release date="2023-09-25" version="2.48" title="Repository Storage Tags">
    <release-core-list>
        <release-bug-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="2182"/>
                <github-pull-request id="2184"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="burak.yurdakul"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                    <release-item-tester id="burak.yurdakul"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Fix issue restoring block incremental without a block list.</p>

                <p>A block map with no blocks, which is written when a file timestamp changes but the file does not, was not decrypted when it followed a file stored without block incremental in the same bundle read. With enough affected files the retries were exhausted and the restore failed.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-bug-list>

        <release-feature-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="2150"/>
                <github-pull-request id="2159"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stefan.fercot"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="timothee.peignier"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Add <br-option>--repo-storage-tag</br-option> option to create object tags.</p>

                <p>Set <setting>repo-storage-tag</setting> to add tags to the objects written to an <proper>S3</proper>, <proper>GCS</proper>, or <proper>Azure</proper> repository. Tags are set for each repository.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2125"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="reid.thompson"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Add known hosts checking for <proper>SFTP</proper> storage driver.</p>

                <p><proper>SFTP</proper> host keys are now checked against the known hosts files by default, i.e. <br-option>repo-sftp-host-key-check-type=strict</br-option>. Set <br-option>repo-sftp-host-key-check-type=accept-new</br-option> to add new hosts automatically, or <br-option>repo-sftp-host-key-check-type=none</br-option> to skip the check as before.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <commit subject="Adjust Wait object to be more accurate when nested."/>
                <commit subject="Aggregate error retries in ErrorRetry output."/>
                <commit subject="Refactor address list lookup to include all returned addresses.">
                    <github-pull-request id="2174"/>
                </commit>
                <commit subject="Support for dual stack connections.">
                    <github-issue id="2154"/>
                    <github-pull-request id="2175"/>
                </commit>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Support for dual stack connections.</p>

                <p>Each address a host name resolves to is now tried in turn, e.g. an IPv6 address with no route to the host and then an IPv4 address, until one connects or the timeout expires. Repeated retry errors are also summarized in error messages.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-issue id="2007"/>
                <github-pull-request id="2141"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="stefan.fercot"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Add backup size completed/total to <cmd>info</cmd> command <proper>JSON</proper> output.</p>

                <p>The JSON output of the <cmd>info</cmd> command now includes the completed and total size of a backup in progress, so progress can be monitored by other programs.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-feature-list>

        <release-improvement-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2057"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Multi-stanza check command.</p>

                <p>When <setting>stanza</setting> is not specified, the <cmd>check</cmd> command now checks every stanza in the configuration.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2131"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stefan.fercot"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Retry reads of <file>pg_control</file> until checksum is valid.</p>

                <p>On some filesystems, e.g. ext4, a read of <file>pg_control</file> during a concurrent write can return torn data. The read is now retried until the checksum is valid.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2169"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Optimize WAL segment check after successful backup.</p>

                <p>The check for WAL segments after a backup listed the storage once for each segment. Each WAL directory is now listed once and the list is reused.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2162"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="reid.thompson"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Improve <proper>GCS</proper> multi-part performance.</p>

                <p>Chunks of a multi-part upload are now uploaded as soon as they are available.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="tom.swartz"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.christensen"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="reid.thompson"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Allow <cmd>archive-get</cmd> command to run when stanza is stopped.</p>

                <p>The <cmd>archive-get</cmd> command does not write to the repository, so it can now run while the stanza is stopped, as <cmd>restore</cmd> can.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2136"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="reid.thompson"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Accept leading tilde in paths for SFTP public/private keys.</p>

                <p>Paths for <setting>repo-sftp-private-key-file</setting> and <setting>repo-sftp-public-key-file</setting> may now begin with <path>~</path>, as documented.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2072"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-ideator id="daniel.farina"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Reload GCS credentials before renewing authentication token.</p>

                <p>The service key file is now read again before the authentication token is renewed, so the key can be replaced while a command is running.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-improvement-list>

        <release-development-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2176"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="stephen.frost"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Add report option to <cmd>check</cmd> command.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Update config.guess and config.sub to latest versions.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Update xxHash to v0.8.2.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <commit subject="Remove UNCONSTIFY() from gz compression module."/>
                <commit subject="Adjust range check per Coverity complaint."/>
                <commit subject="Refactor IoRead handling in backupFile()."/>
                <commit subject="Encode key in HTTP query."/>
                <commit subject="Add missing const qualifier to errorTypeList."/>
                <commit subject="Use PROJECT_NAME constant instead of string literal."/>
                <commit subject="Add missing comma in protocolParallelJobToLog()."/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                    <release-item-contributor id="reid.thompson"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Clean up code.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Finalize catalog number for PostgreSQL 16 release.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Add prefix to meson build target to avoid conflicts.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Fix manifest command filter for files in a tablespace.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Add block incremental info to restore detail logging.</p>
            </release-item>
        </release-development-list>
    </release-core-list>

    <release-doc-list>
        <release-bug-list>
            <release-item>
                <github-pull-request id="2165"/>

                <release-item-contributor-list>
                    <release-item-contributor id="hartmut.goebel"/>
                    <release-item-reviewer id="david.steele"/>
                </release-item-contributor-list>

                <p>Fix configuration reference example for the <br-option>tls-server-address</br-option> option.</p>

                <p>The example <id>::*</id> was not valid. Use <id>*</id> for IPv4 or <id>::</id> for IPv6.</p>
            </release-item>

            <release-item>
                <release-item-contributor-list>
